      "criticality": "CORE",
      "provenance": {
        "source_file": "tasks/motion_video_task2/instruction.md",
        "source_type": "instruction",
        "line_start": 1,
        "line_end": 1,
        "exact_text": "I am a math education content creator, and I want to produce an educational video explaining Fourier series convergence. Please analyze the Fourier series of a square wave: f(x)=1 for 0<x<\\pi, f(x)=-1 for -\\pi<x<0, with period 2\\pi.\n",
        "source_sha256": "f288e0c136fe155789a48b5c5d204a11d165eed4455fed3c902de157ee922896",
        "extraction_rule": "actionable_paragraph"
      }
    },
    {
      "requirement_id": "req_ada0e9e461f4b7d6ee54",
      "requirement_type": "DOMAIN_ACTION",
      "criticality": "HARD",
      "provenance": {
        "source_file": "tasks/motion_video_task2/instruction.md",
        "source_type": "instruction",
        "line_start": 3,
        "line_end": 3,
        "exact_text": "Compute the Fourier coefficients b_n for n=1 to n=10 (exactly 10 coefficients, do NOT include a_0). Also compute partial sums for N=1, 3, 5, and 10 terms.\n",
        "source_sha256": "f288e0c136fe155789a48b5c5d204a11d165eed4455fed3c902de157ee922896",
        "extraction_rule": "actionable_paragraph"
      }
    },
    {
      "requirement_id": "req_806880d489e78a0e7f89",
      "requirement_type": "DOMAIN_ACTION",
      "criticality": "SUPPORT",
      "provenance": {
        "source_file": "tasks/motion_video_task2/instruction.md",
        "source_type": "instruction",
        "line_start": 6,
        "line_end": 6,
        "exact_text": "- A 'coefficients' array containing exactly 10 objects, each with 'n' (integer 1-10) and 'value' (the b_n coefficient value)\n",
        "source_sha256": "f288e0c136fe155789a48b5c5d204a11d165eed4455fed3c902de157ee922896",
        "extraction_rule": "commonmark_list_item"
      }
    },
    {
      "requirement_id": "req_7446263736a60bae23e1",
      "requirement_type": "DOMAIN_ACTION",
      "criticality": "SUPPORT",
      "provenance": {
        "source_file": "tasks/motion_video_task2/instruction.md",
        "source_type": "instruction",
        "line_start": 7,
        "line_end": 8,
        "exact_text": "- A 'partial_sums' object with keys 'N=1', 'N=3', 'N=5', 'N=10', where each contains an 'expression' field showing the formula using symbolic fractions with π (e.g., '(4/pi)*sin(x) + (4/(3*pi))*sin(3*x)'), not decimal approximations\n\n",
        "source_sha256": "f288e0c136fe155789a48b5c5d204a11d165eed4455fed3c902de157ee922896",
        "extraction_rule": "commonmark_list_item"
      }
    },
    {
      "requirement_id": "req_055244feb9dce14e5b1a",
      "requirement_type": "DOMAIN_ACTION",
      "criticality": "HARD",
      "provenance": {
        "source_file": "tasks/motion_video_task2/instruction.md",
        "source_type": "instruction",
        "line_start": 9,
        "line_end": 9,
        "exact_text": "Then create fourier_animation.mp4 showing the square wave and how the Fourier approximation progressively improves. The animation must show 4 clearly distinct and separate stages for N=1, 3, 5, and 10, with visible transitions between each stage. Display the mathematical formulas (using fractions with π) in the animation. Ensure axis labels use clean formatting without excessive decimal places.",
        "source_sha256": "f288e0c136fe155789a48b5c5d204a11d165eed4455fed3c902de157ee922896",
        "extraction_rule": "actionable_paragraph"
      }
